/// Spike 5: the reply token BT-4090 proposes (`self deferReply ->
/// ReplyTo`), here wrapping the raw `gen_server` `From` that the
/// throwaway native connection hands to `ConnLogic`. A plain Value:
/// storable in a Dictionary, usable from any later message. Replies go
/// out with `gen_server:reply/2` through the FFI, in the `{ok, V}` /
/// `{error, E}` shape `beamtalk_actor:sync_send/3` unwraps. Named
/// `SpikeReplyTo` because the stdlib now ships its own `ReplyTo`.
/// Spike-only.
sealed typed Value subclass: SpikeReplyTo
  // gen_server's `From`, `{pid, tag}`.
  field: from :: Tuple = {nil, nil}

  /// Answer the parked caller with `value`. A no-op if the caller has
  /// already timed out or died (OTP: the reply goes to a dead alias).
  reply: value :: Object -> SpikeReplyTo =>
    Erlang gen_server reply: self.from with: {#ok, value}
    self

  /// Make the parked caller's send raise `error`, as a failed sync call.
  replyError: error :: Exception -> SpikeReplyTo =>
    Erlang gen_server reply: self.from with: {#error, error}
    self
